data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":907,"output_index":2,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_03f11f0a7fad75a4016acd22484ba081938c2a8bb8afa61e26","call_id":"call_5fd4f468c76b4053bfa754e046b31b54","name":"edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"server.js\",\"edits\":[{\"oldText\":\"const priorities = ['Low', 'Normal', 'High'];\",\"newText\":\"// Remember positions even while tasks belong to a different project.\\n// Seed current memberships from the previous ordering without rearranging tasks.\\ndb.exec(`\\n  CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS task_positions (\\n    task_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES tasks(id),\\n    project_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES projects(id),\\n    position INTEGER NOT NULL,\\n    PRIMARY KEY (task_id, project_id),\\n    UNIQUE (project_id, position)\\n  );\\n  INSERT OR IGNORE INTO task_positions (task_id, project_id, position)\\n    SELECT id, project_id, sort_order FROM tasks;\\n`);\\nconst priorities = ['Low', 'Normal', 'High'];\"},{\"oldText\":\"const createTask = db.prepare('INSERT INTO tasks (project_id, title, priority, sort_order) VALUES (?, ?, ?, (SELECT COALESCE(MAX(sort_order), 0) + 1 FROM tasks))');\\nconst moveTask = db.prepare('UPDATE tasks SET project_id = ?, sort_order = (SELECT COALESCE(MAX(sort_order), 0) + 1 FROM tasks) WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?');\",\"newText\":\"const insertTask = db.prepare('INSERT INTO tasks (project_id, title, priority, sort_order) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)');\\nconst nextPosition = db.prepare('SELECT COALESCE(MAX(position), 0) + 1 AS position FROM task_positions WHERE project_id = ?');\\nconst rememberPosition = db.prepare('INSERT OR IGNORE INTO task_positions (task_id, project_id, position) VALUES (?, ?, ?)');\\nconst getPosition = db.prepare('SELECT position FROM task_positions WHERE task_id = ? AND project_id = ?');\\nconst getOwnedTask = db.prepare('SELECT id FROM tasks WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?');\\nconst relocateTask = db.prepare('UPDATE tasks SET project_id = ?, sort_order = ? WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?');\\n\\nfunction transaction(operation) {\\n  db.exec('BEGIN IMMEDIATE');\\n  try {\\n    const result = operation();\\n    db.exec('COMMIT');\\n    return result;\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    db.exec('ROLLBACK');\\n    throw error;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction createTask(projectId, title, priority) {\\n  return transaction(() => {\\n    const { position } = nextPosition.get(projectId);\\n    const result = insertTask.run(projectId, title, priority, position);\\n    rememberPosition.run(result.lastInsertRowid, projectId, position);\\n    return result;\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nfunction moveTask(destinationId, taskId, sourceId) {\\n  return transaction(() => {\\n    if (!getOwnedTask.get(taskId, sourceId)) return { changes: 0 };\\n    const remembered = getPosition.get(taskId, destinationId);\\n    const position = remembered?.position ?? nextPosition.get(destinationId).position;\\n    if (!remembered) rememberPosition.run(taskId, destinationId, position);\\n    return relocateTask.run(destinationId, position, taskId, sourceId);\\n  });\\n}\"},{\"oldText\":\"result = moveTask.run(destination.id, taskId, projectId);\",\"newText\":\"result = moveTask(destination.id, taskId, projectId);\"},{\"oldText\":\"createTask.run(projectId, title, project.default_priority);\",\"newText\":\"createTask(projectId, title, project.default_priority);\"}]}","status":"completed"}}

event: response.completed
data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":908,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_03f11f0a7fad75a4016acd224217748193b6ef1b30a55ffc8a","object":"response","created_at":1791828546,"completed_at":1791828565,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<addendum>\nKeep changes focused and readable. Use clear names and avoid needless duplication. Verify the changed behavior with appropriate checks before submitting.\n</addendum>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_03f11f0a7fad75a4016acd224377d88193ba7983fa0475ba10","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Evaluating positions table management**\n\nI need to decide whether to keep the sort_order cache for my positions table or remove it entirely. I want to ensure that each project maintains a unique position. When migrating, I should insert any missing current tasks at the start, using a safe, transactional approach to avoid ghost entries. The wrapper function for transactions needs to be generic. I’ll initialize from the sort_order ranks and ensure t